Fix Wi-Fi -12 (ENOMEM) on AI-VOX3: retry esp_malloc_internal() from internal
SRAM instead of failing when kmm_malloc() returns a PSRAM block.

===========================================================================
ROOT CAUSE (verified against real hardware, run#135)
===========================================================================

Symptom: esp32s3_wlan_sta_initialize() returns -12 (-ENOMEM); the board gets
no IP and can never reach the PC voice bridge.  Call chain:

  esp32s3_wlan_sta_initialize()     arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_wlan.c:1663
    -> esp_wifi_adapter_init()      arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_wifi_adapter.c:4625
      -> esp_wifi_init(&wifi_cfg)   returns ESP_ERR_NO_MEM
        -> wifi_errno_trans()       same file, :615  ->  -ENOMEM

Wi-Fi allocates its DMA buffers through esp_malloc_internal().  In a flat
build (no CONFIG_MM_KERNEL_HEAP, no CONFIG_XTENSA_IMEM_USE_SEPARATE_HEAP) that
function used to be:

    void *ptr = kmm_malloc(size);
    if (ptr != NULL)
      {
        if (esp32s3_ptr_extram(ptr))
          {
            kmm_free(ptr);
            return NULL;          <-- gives up after ONE attempt
          }
      }
    return ptr;

Wi-Fi DMA buffers MUST live in internal SRAM.  With
CONFIG_ESP32S3_SPIRAM_COMMON_HEAP=y (which is forced: ESP32S3_SPIRAM_HEAP is a
choice whose flat-build default is COMMON_HEAP -- esp32s3/Kconfig:1025-1040)
the 8 MB PSRAM is folded into the ordinary heap, so kmm_malloc() very often
hands back a PSRAM block.  That block is rejected as external RAM, freed, and
NULL returned -> esp_wifi_init() sees ESP_ERR_NO_MEM -> -ENOMEM.

The bigger the heap, the more likely a PSRAM block is chosen, so "enabling
PSRAM" made Wi-Fi LESS likely to work -- a self-defeating knot.

===========================================================================
WHY NOT JUST TURN SPIRAM_COMMON_HEAP OFF
===========================================================================

It is a choice and cannot be deselected in a flat build.  Writing
"# CONFIG_ESP32S3_SPIRAM_COMMON_HEAP is not set" in the defconfig does not
deselect a choice: olddefconfig restores the default and the CI config audit
still sees =y.  Verified on run#136, which printed "CONFIG AUDIT OK" with
COMMON_HEAP=y even though the defconfig said "is not set".

===========================================================================
THE FIX
===========================================================================

Retry: when kmm_malloc() returns a PSRAM block, free it and ask again, up to
ESP_WIFI_IRAM_ALLOC_RETRIES (64) times.  Internal-SRAM blocks are returned
immediately.  The loop is strictly bounded so it can never wedge the boot
(this runs during board init).

If every attempt still lands in PSRAM we return NULL exactly as before, so the
failure mode is unchanged (loud -ENOMEM) rather than silently wrong.

On success Wi-Fi gets exactly the DMA-capable buffer it requires, while the
8 MB PSRAM stays in the ordinary heap for the application -- which needs it
for the 768 KB TTS PCM sink (AIVOX3_TTS_PCM_MAX_BYTES).

Generated from a real edit and validated with BOTH `git apply --check` and
`patch -p1 --dry-run --forward` (CI uses `patch -p1`).
--- a/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_wifi_adapter.c
+++ b/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/esp32s3_wifi_adapter.c
@@ -92,6 +92,19 @@
  * Pre-processor Definitions
  ****************************************************************************/
 
+/* AI-VOX3 FIX (2026-10-17): how many times esp_malloc_internal() retries
+ * after kmm_malloc() hands back a PSRAM (external RAM) block.  Wi-Fi DMA
+ * buffers must live in internal SRAM, and with the 8 MB PSRAM folded into
+ * the ordinary heap a single attempt very often lands in external RAM --
+ * which used to abort the whole Wi-Fi init with -ENOMEM.  64 attempts is
+ * generous (each is a cheap alloc/free pair) yet strictly bounded, so a
+ * pathological allocator can never wedge the boot.
+ */
+
+#ifndef ESP_WIFI_IRAM_ALLOC_RETRIES
+#  define ESP_WIFI_IRAM_ALLOC_RETRIES 64
+#endif
+
 #define PHY_RF_MASK   ((1 << PHY_BT_MODULE) | (1 << PHY_WIFI_MODULE))
 
 #define WIFI_CONNECT_TIMEOUT  CONFIG_ESP32S3_WIFI_CONNECT_TIMEOUT
@@ -3356,18 +3369,36 @@
 #elif defined(CONFIG_XTENSA_IMEM_USE_SEPARATE_HEAP)
   return xtensa_imm_malloc(size);
 #else
-  void *ptr = kmm_malloc(size);
+  /* AI-VOX3 FIX (2026-10-17): Wi-Fi's DMA buffers must come from internal
+   * SRAM.  With the 8 MB PSRAM folded into the ordinary heap
+   * (CONFIG_ESP32S3_SPIRAM_COMMON_HEAP) kmm_malloc() frequently returns a
+   * PSRAM block, which used to be freed and reported as a hard failure --
+   * esp_wifi_init() then died with ESP_ERR_NO_MEM and
+   * esp32s3_wlan_sta_initialize() returned -12.  Retry instead: free the
+   * external block and ask again, so the allocator gets a chance to serve
+   * the request from internal SRAM.  Bounded, so it cannot wedge boot.
+   */
+
+  int  retry;
+  void *ptr;
 
-  if (ptr != NULL)
+  for (retry = 0; retry < ESP_WIFI_IRAM_ALLOC_RETRIES; retry++)
     {
-      if (esp32s3_ptr_extram(ptr))
+      ptr = kmm_malloc(size);
+      if (ptr == NULL)
         {
-          kmm_free(ptr);
           return NULL;
         }
+
+      if (!esp32s3_ptr_extram(ptr))
+        {
+          return ptr;   /* internal SRAM: exactly what DMA needs */
+        }
+
+      kmm_free(ptr);    /* external RAM: not usable, try again */
     }
 
-  return ptr;
+  return NULL;
 #endif
 }
 
